# {{SYSTEM_NAME}} Engineering Agents — Claude Code Handoff

Orchestration layer for the **code** arm of {{PROJECT_NAME}}. This context turns the Figma design system
and the validated screens into **shipping software**: the one coded component library ({{COMPONENT_LIB}})
+ Storybook, the {{APP_KIND}} ({{APP_STACK}}), and the release. It is the third context alongside
`{{DS_REPO}}` (Figma DS) and `{{STUDIO_REPO}}` (Figma screens + prototype).

> **Platform: `{{PLATFORM}}`.** The roster and the pipeline below are the same on either platform; the
> `developer` and `release-engineer` bodies, their commands, and the release runbook are the `{{PLATFORM}}`
> variants. Switch by changing `engineering.platform` in the template config and re-rendering.

---

## The organizing principle — one coded library, three consumers

The Figma DS is authored in `{{DS_REPO}}`. **This** context builds its ONE code implementation and ships
it. `{{COMPONENT_LIB}}` is consumed by (1) Storybook, (2) {{PROTO_CONSUMER}}, and (3) the {{APP_KIND}} —
so the thing you usability-test is the thing you ship. That shared library is what makes prototype→app
rework near-zero.

| Role | Write surface | Owns (object type) |
|---|---|---|
| `design-system-engineer` | `{{ENGINEERING_REPO}}` — `{{COMPONENT_LIB}}` ({{COMPONENT_KIND}} + coded tokens) + Storybook | the CODE mirror of {{SYSTEM_NAME}} — token sync from the Figma DS, components, stories, code↔Figma parity |
| `developer` | `{{ENGINEERING_REPO}}` — the {{APP_KIND}} ({{APP_STACK}}, {{APP_ID_LABEL}} `{{APP_ID}}`) | screens composed from the shared library · navigation · state/data · platform integration · {{VERIFY_GATE}} verification |
| `release-engineer` | `{{ENGINEERING_REPO}}` — build/release config, environment, promotion | the {{DEPLOY_UNIT}} · versioning · public declarations · deploy to {{RELEASE_TARGET}} |

**Mental model:** `design-system-engineer` codes the DS as `{{COMPONENT_LIB}}` (token-synced, Storybook-
verified) → the studio's prototype and `developer`'s app both consume it → `developer` wires
platform concerns onto the validated screens → `release-engineer` builds, ships, and CONFIRMS the release.
A Figma DS gap routes to `{{DS_REPO}}`; a design/flow change routes to `{{STUDIO_REPO}}`.

