## Cross-context seams (where this context connects)

```
{{DS_REPO}} (Figma DS) ──published tokens + component keys──▶ design-system-engineer (token sync + {{COMPONENT_LIB}})
                                                                        │  publishes {{COMPONENT_LIB}}
                        ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┐
                        ▼                                                                                 ▼
{{STUDIO_REPO}}: validated screens ──▶ prototype (consumes {{COMPONENT_LIB}})                    developer ({{APP_KIND}})
                        │                          usability gate (product-designer + data-analyst)         │
                        └──────────────── validated flow is the app's spec ─────────────────────────────────┘
                                                                                                            ▼
                                                                                        release-engineer ({{RELEASE_TARGET}})
```

- **From `{{DS_REPO}}`:** published tokens + component keys → `design-system-engineer` regenerates coded
  tokens + builds/updates components. A missing token/component is a DS gap, filed there.
- **From `{{STUDIO_REPO}}`:** the validated screen specs + acceptance criteria are `developer`'s build
  input; the prototype (which the studio owns as the usability gate) consumes `{{COMPONENT_LIB}}` so it is
  faithful to the app.
- **Back to the design contexts:** a component can't do what a screen needs → `design-system-engineer` builds
  it (code) or files a Figma DS gap (design); a flow doesn't work in code → back to `{{STUDIO_REPO}}`.

